+## 2026-11-26 — AUDIT-NEXT-A: what the two checks of AUDIT-WIRE left open in the audit module
+
+Only `src/audit.rs` changed in the daemon's source; with `--audit` absent the daemon behaves exactly as before. A session
+whose audit log could not be created now keeps that failure's reason in `status.audit`, followed by what to do (end the
+session and pair again), instead of having it replaced by "missing or empty" at the first send; the log is still never
+created twice in one session (the owner's ruling). The seal's last step is one function that can be driven without a
+host: a host left without its member is opened again once before the seal gives up, and a seal that landed but could
+not reopen the log now says so. "Nothing could be filed" now says which cause the daemon can see (nothing new, or the
+checkpoint could not be written), and keeps the old wording when it cannot tell. The "unavailable" seal reply gained
+`limits: null`; three "give the command again" texts now say to fix the cause first. AW-7 now fails on its own
+message. Four red rows (`AN-1` to `AN-3`). Still open for a later lane: F-2, F-4, N-3, the email-masking ruling (N-6).
